<title>LEBANON: Short-term T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Short-term T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields on short-term Lebanese treasury bills for the June 26 issue fell while long-term t-bill yields held steady, the Bank of Lebanon said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following rate details (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				 percent)		    (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	   12.97 (13.01)		13.40 (13.45)</p>
<p>    Six months	     13.27 (13.33)		14.21 (14.28)</p>
<p>    12 month		 13.20 (13.20)		15.20 (15.20)</p>
<p>    24 month   (interest payable twice early)     16.08 (16.08)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
